{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.genus_ideal_characterisation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.genus_ideal_characterisation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Ideal.Span","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Ideal.Maps","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Ideal.Quotient.Operations","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Ideal.Quotient.Defs"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.genus_ideal_characterisation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.genus_ideal_characterisation","kind":"theorem","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/genus_ideal_characterisation.lean#L33-L52","doc":"**Genus-filtration ideal characterisation** at `g = 4`.\n\nThe kernel of the canonical quotient map\n`ℤ[u] → ℤ[u] / (u⁵)` is the principal ideal `(u⁵)`.  This is the\nabstract ring-theoretic core of the genus-filtration content\ndescribed in `lem:genus-ideal-characterisation`; the categorical\nSeifert-cycle interpretation of the same ideal is recorded in the\nmanuscript.\n\nDischarged by the standard `Ideal.mk_ker` identity (kernel of the\nquotient projection equals the ideal we quotient by). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:lem:genus-ideal-characterisation","label":"lem:genus-ideal-characterisation","md":"quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/genus-ideal-characterisation.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}